IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp6-information`

-- Tests of cp6-information.l4 (sections 104.1 to 107, lines 2731 to 2777 of the Act file).

§ `Tests -- information, agreements and oaths`

§§ `Section 104.1(1): which bodies' public officers may hold and be given the information`

-- Source bodies: the Canada Revenue Agency, Finance, Public Works and Government Services, Citizenship and Immigration.
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) — the body is one whose public officer may make the information available` `the Canada Revenue Agency`
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) — the body is one whose public officer may make the information available` `the Department of Finance`
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) — the body is one whose public officer may make the information available` `the Department of Public Works and Government Services`
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) — the body is one whose public officer may make the information available` `the Department of Citizenship and Immigration`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 104.1(1) — the body is one whose public officer may make the information available` `the Department of Employment and Social Development`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 104.1(1) — the body is one whose public officer may make the information available` `the Office of the Superintendent of Financial Institutions`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 104.1(1) — the body is one whose public officer may make the information available` `another body`)
-- Recipient bodies: those four, and also Employment and Social Development and the Superintendent.
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) — the body is one whose public officer may be given the information` `the Canada Revenue Agency`
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) — the body is one whose public officer may be given the information` `the Department of Finance`
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) — the body is one whose public officer may be given the information` `the Department of Public Works and Government Services`
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) — the body is one whose public officer may be given the information` `the Department of Citizenship and Immigration`
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) — the body is one whose public officer may be given the information` `the Department of Employment and Social Development`
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) — the body is one whose public officer may be given the information` `the Office of the Superintendent of Financial Institutions`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 104.1(1) — the body is one whose public officer may be given the information` `another body`)

-- Inputs: holder's body; holder is a public officer; obtained for the purpose of the administration; recipient's body; recipient is a public officer; made available for that purpose.
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) — the information may be made available despite any other Act or law` `the Canada Revenue Agency` TRUE TRUE `the Department of Employment and Social Development` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) — the information may be made available despite any other Act or law` `the Department of Finance` TRUE TRUE `the Department of Citizenship and Immigration` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) — the information may be made available despite any other Act or law` `the Department of Citizenship and Immigration` TRUE TRUE `the Office of the Superintendent of Financial Institutions` TRUE TRUE
-- The Department of Employment and Social Development is a recipient only, not a source.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 104.1(1) — the information may be made available despite any other Act or law` `the Department of Employment and Social Development` TRUE TRUE `the Canada Revenue Agency` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 104.1(1) — the information may be made available despite any other Act or law` `another body` TRUE TRUE `the Canada Revenue Agency` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 104.1(1) — the information may be made available despite any other Act or law` `the Canada Revenue Agency` TRUE TRUE `another body` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 104.1(1) — the information may be made available despite any other Act or law` `the Canada Revenue Agency` FALSE TRUE `the Department of Finance` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 104.1(1) — the information may be made available despite any other Act or law` `the Canada Revenue Agency` TRUE FALSE `the Department of Finance` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 104.1(1) — the information may be made available despite any other Act or law` `the Canada Revenue Agency` TRUE TRUE `the Department of Finance` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 104.1(1) — the information may be made available despite any other Act or law` `the Canada Revenue Agency` TRUE TRUE `the Department of Finance` TRUE FALSE)

§§ `Section 104.1(2): no further, unless for the same purpose and on the Minister's conditions`

-- Inputs: obtained under section 104.1; the recipient is other than a public officer of a named body; only for the same purpose; on the Minister's conditions.
#ASSERT `s 104.1(2) — the information obtained under section 104.1 may be made available to the other person or body` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 104.1(2) — the information obtained under section 104.1 may be made available to the other person or body` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 104.1(2) — the information obtained under section 104.1 may be made available to the other person or body` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered: information not obtained under section 104.1, or passed to a named body's public officer.
#ASSERT `s 104.1(2) — the information obtained under section 104.1 may be made available to the other person or body` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 104.1(2) — the information obtained under section 104.1 may be made available to the other person or body` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 105: agreement with a province`

`cp6 test province providing a comprehensive pension plan` MEANS Province WITH
    `name of the province` IS "Test province A"
    `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS TRUE

`cp6 test province not providing a comprehensive pension plan` MEANS Province WITH
    `name of the province` IS "Test province B"
    `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 105 — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the province about records and information` `cp6 test province providing a comprehensive pension plan`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 105 — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the province about records and information` `cp6 test province not providing a comprehensive pension plan`)

-- Inputs: the direction; the agreement is in force; obtained under the holder's plan; made available under prescribed conditions; made available on a reciprocal basis.
#ASSERT `s 105(a) — information may be made available under the agreement` `from the Minister to the appropriate authority of the province` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 105(a) — information may be made available under the agreement` `from the Minister to the appropriate authority of the province` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 105(a) — information may be made available under the agreement` `from the appropriate authority of the province to the Minister` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 105(a) — information may be made available under the agreement` `from the appropriate authority of the province to the Minister` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 105(a) — information may be made available under the agreement` `from the Minister to the appropriate authority of the province` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 105(a) — information may be made available under the agreement` `from the Minister to the appropriate authority of the province` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- Inputs: the agreement is in force; the individual has made contributions under this Act and the provincial plan; the agreement's terms and conditions are met.
#ASSERT `s 105(b) — a statement of the amounts shown to the individual's account may be made available by the Minister or the provincial authority` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 105(b) — a statement of the amounts shown to the individual's account may be made available by the Minister or the provincial authority` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 105(b) — a statement of the amounts shown to the individual's account may be made available by the Minister or the provincial authority` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 105(b) — a statement of the amounts shown to the individual's account may be made available by the Minister or the provincial authority` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- ... and a request for reconsideration of such a statement.
#ASSERT `s 105(b) — the Minister or the provincial authority may act on the individual's request for reconsideration` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 105(b) — the Minister or the provincial authority may act on the individual's request for reconsideration` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 105(b) — the Minister or the provincial authority may act on the individual's request for reconsideration` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)

§§ `Section 106: oaths, affidavits, declarations and solemn affirmations`

-- Inputs: the authorized person's kind; acts in the course of employment; another Act limits the power.
#ASSERT `s 106(1) — the authorized person may administer oaths, take affidavits, declarations and solemn affirmations, and has the powers of a commissioner for taking affidavits` `employed in the administration or enforcement of Part I or its regulations and authorized by the Minister of National Revenue` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 106(1) — the authorized person may administer oaths, take affidavits, declarations and solemn affirmations, and has the powers of a commissioner for taking affidavits` `employed in the administration or enforcement of Part III and Part II or their regulations and authorized by the Minister` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 106(1) — the authorized person may administer oaths, take affidavits, declarations and solemn affirmations, and has the powers of a commissioner for taking affidavits` `neither of those` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 106(1) — the authorized person may administer oaths, take affidavits, declarations and solemn affirmations, and has the powers of a commissioner for taking affidavits` `employed in the administration or enforcement of Part I or its regulations and authorized by the Minister of National Revenue` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered: another Act of Parliament or of a provincial legislature limits the power; that Act is not read here.
#ASSERT `s 106(1) — the authorized person may administer oaths, take affidavits, declarations and solemn affirmations, and has the powers of a commissioner for taking affidavits` `employed in the administration or enforcement of Part I or its regulations and authorized by the Minister of National Revenue` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Inputs: the accepting person's kind; for the purposes of the Part or regulations its own paragraph names; the maker is a listed officer or employee; the maker has the powers of a commissioner.
#ASSERT `s 106(2) — the authorized person may accept the oath, affidavit, declaration or solemn affirmation` `employed in the administration or enforcement of Part I or its regulations and authorized by the Minister of National Revenue` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 106(2) — the authorized person may accept the oath, affidavit, declaration or solemn affirmation` `employed in the administration or enforcement of Part III and Part II or their regulations and authorized by the Minister` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 106(2) — the authorized person may accept the oath, affidavit, declaration or solemn affirmation` `neither of those` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 106(2) — the authorized person may accept the oath, affidavit, declaration or solemn affirmation` `employed in the administration or enforcement of Part I or its regulations and authorized by the Minister of National Revenue` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 106(2) — the authorized person may accept the oath, affidavit, declaration or solemn affirmation` `employed in the administration or enforcement of Part I or its regulations and authorized by the Minister of National Revenue` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 106(2) — the authorized person may accept the oath, affidavit, declaration or solemn affirmation` `employed in the administration or enforcement of Part I or its regulations and authorized by the Minister of National Revenue` TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§§ `Section 107: reciprocal agreements with other countries`

-- Inputs: a law of the other country provides benefits; the Governor in Council approves the terms.
#ASSERT `s 107(1) — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the other country` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 107(1) — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the other country` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 107(1) — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the other country` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 107(1) — the agreement may make the arrangement` `the exchange of information obtained under that law or this Act`
#ASSERT `s 107(1) — the agreement may make the arrangement` `the administration of benefits payable under this Act to persons resident in that country, and their extension, increase or decrease`
#ASSERT `s 107(1) — the agreement may make the arrangement` `the administration of benefits payable under that law to persons resident in Canada, and their extension, increase or decrease`
#ASSERT `s 107(1) — the agreement may make the arrangement` `another arrangement relating to the administration or operation of that law and of this Act`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 107(1) — the agreement may make the arrangement` `an arrangement that does not relate to the administration or operation of either`)
#ASSERT `s 107(1) — the agreement may extend to a similar arrangement about a provincial pension plan` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 107(1) — the agreement may extend to a similar arrangement about a provincial pension plan` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 107(1) — the agreement may extend to a similar arrangement about a provincial pension plan` FALSE TRUE)

-- Inputs: an agreement is in force; the person is employed in or resident in the other country; the person is employed in or resident in Canada.
#ASSERT `s 107(1)(b) and (c) — the agreement may provide for the benefits payable to or in respect of the person to be extended, increased or decreased` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 107(1)(b) and (c) — the agreement may provide for the benefits payable to or in respect of the person to be extended, increased or decreased` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 107(1)(b) and (c) — the agreement may provide for the benefits payable to or in respect of the person to be extended, increased or decreased` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 107(1)(b) and (c) — the agreement may provide for the benefits payable to or in respect of the person to be extended, increased or decreased` FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- Inputs: the province; the province has requested; the Governor in Council approves; a law of the other country provides benefits; the provincial plan makes provision.
#ASSERT `s 107(4) — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the other country about the provincial pension plan` `cp6 test province providing a comprehensive pension plan` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 107(4) — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the other country about the provincial pension plan` `cp6 test province not providing a comprehensive pension plan` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 107(4) — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the other country about the provincial pension plan` `cp6 test province providing a comprehensive pension plan` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 107(4) — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the other country about the provincial pension plan` `cp6 test province providing a comprehensive pension plan` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 107(4) — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the other country about the provincial pension plan` `cp6 test province providing a comprehensive pension plan` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 107(4) — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the other country about the provincial pension plan` `cp6 test province providing a comprehensive pension plan` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
